Modifications by Alpha-Leader, 2026-07-28
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Correctness fixes:

  * Icon retrieval used a blocking SendMessageW(WM_GETICON), which never
    returned if the target application was not pumping its message queue. A
    single hung window permanently froze the window list with no recovery,
    including via the F5 refresh. Replaced with a time-bounded
    SendMessageTimeoutW, and the refresh flag is now released by an RAII guard
    so no exit path can strand it.

  * The selected window was tracked by its index into a list that is rebuilt
    and re-sorted every five seconds, so a reordering between selection and
    action could apply changes to a different application. Selection is now
    tracked by window handle.

  * Window handles were used without validation. Because Windows recycles
    handles, a stale entry could target an unrelated window. Handles are now
    checked with IsWindow before any modification.

  * Restoring borders OR-ed in WS_CAPTION | WS_THICKFRAME rather than replaying
    the window's actual previous style, which gave dialogs and natively
    borderless windows frames they never had. The original style, rectangle,
    and topmost state are now recorded and restored exactly.

  * Process names were resolved with a full CreateToolhelp32Snapshot per window
    per refresh, and the snapshot handle was never closed. Replaced with a
    single snapshot per refresh that is properly closed.

New features:

  * Region placement: a stripped window can be sized and anchored into a
    sub-rectangle of a monitor (centered, left, right, or a custom offset)
    rather than only filling the entire display. Intended for fitting a game
    into part of an ultrawide monitor.

  * Optional always-on-top, which is what allows a window narrower than the
    monitor to cover the taskbar.

  * Settings persist to %APPDATA%\ultraborderless\config.txt.

  * Action results and failures are surfaced in the UI; previously they were
    written to a console that does not exist in a windowed subsystem build.

  * Unit tests covering placement geometry and style round-tripping.

